1
00:00:08,255 --> 00:00:18,748
Long long ago, in the island of Lanka,
South of ancient India, lived the evil king Ravana...

2
00:00:18,909 --> 00:00:23,869
...whose wicked ambition to
conquer and dominate the...

3
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,878
...whole world, caused pain
and misery to one and all.

4
00:00:28,084 --> 00:00:31,884
And in Kaushala,
a kingdom in north India...

5
00:00:32,088 --> 00:00:35,888
...people prospered under
the benevolent ruler, Dashrath.

6
00:00:39,095 --> 00:00:41,893
However, Kaushala's capital
Ayodhya's biggest concern...

7
00:00:42,098 --> 00:00:44,896
...was that King Dashrath
had no heir.

8
00:00:46,937 --> 00:00:49,906
On the advice of
sage Vashishtha...

9
00:00:50,106 --> 00:00:52,904
...King Dashrath
performed a Yajna...

10
00:00:53,109 --> 00:00:54,906
...the ceremony
to beget a son.

11
00:00:55,946 --> 00:00:58,915
And as a result he was
blessed with four sons...

12
00:00:59,115 --> 00:01:00,912
...from his three queens.

13
00:01:02,118 --> 00:01:03,915
One of them was Ram...

14
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:05,917
...the hero of this story...

15
00:01:06,122 --> 00:01:09,922
...born of Dashrath's
first queen, Kaushalya.

16
00:01:12,963 --> 00:01:14,931
Whenever there have
been crises on the earth...

17
00:01:15,131 --> 00:01:16,928
...Lord Vishnu has
descended from the heavens...

18
00:01:17,133 --> 00:01:18,930
...for its salvation.

19
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:22,939
Lord Vishnu has
ten incarnations...

20
00:01:23,139 --> 00:01:26,939
...and Ram is believed to
be his seventh incarnation.

21
00:01:28,979 --> 00:01:30,947
When Ram turned fifteen...

22
00:01:31,147 --> 00:01:33,945
...Ravan was at
the peak of his powers.

23
00:01:34,985 --> 00:01:36,953
Ravan's relation, Marich...

24
00:01:37,153 --> 00:01:38,950
...along with his mother Tadaka...

25
00:01:39,155 --> 00:01:42,955
...was a terror for sage
Vishwamitra and other hermits...

26
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:47,545
...who lived in a forest
close to Ayodhya's border.

27
00:01:48,804 --> 00:01:51,726
They disturbed Vishwamitra's
prayers, every day.

28
00:01:52,812 --> 00:01:54,867
And on one such day...

29
00:03:04,066 --> 00:03:05,943
O Lord Vishnu...

30
00:03:06,157 --> 00:03:10,125
...is there no one who can
save us from this torment?

31
00:03:12,428 --> 00:03:14,305
His name is Ram.

32
00:03:15,391 --> 00:03:19,525
First born prince of
King Dashrath, of Ayodhya.

33
00:04:16,192 --> 00:04:18,068
O sage of sages...

34
00:04:18,282 --> 00:04:21,204
...my court is indeed
blessed by your presence.

35
00:04:21,418 --> 00:04:23,295
What is it that
you desire of me?

36
00:04:23,509 --> 00:04:25,385
Let me fulfill your command!

37
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:28,521
O noble king of
the Solar Dynasty...

38
00:04:28,735 --> 00:04:31,657
...the demons ruined
the sacred land...

39
00:04:32,743 --> 00:04:34,798
...and we are in great trouble.
I need your...

40
00:04:35,007 --> 00:04:36,884
...eldest son Ram to destroy them.

41
00:04:41,279 --> 00:04:44,201
Ram!? He is but a mere boy.

42
00:04:44,415 --> 00:04:47,337
I, myself, shall wipe them
off from the face of this earth.

43
00:04:47,551 --> 00:04:49,427
This is a command from the Gods...

44
00:04:49,641 --> 00:04:52,563
...O King, do you dare reject it?

45
00:04:52,777 --> 00:04:54,654
Dashrath, send your sons...

46
00:04:54,868 --> 00:04:56,744
...Ram and Lakshman.

47
00:04:56,959 --> 00:04:58,835
Vishwamitra is strong and wise...

48
00:04:59,921 --> 00:05:01,976
...and has mastery
over every weapon.

49
00:05:02,185 --> 00:05:04,062
He will protect your sons.

50
00:05:07,412 --> 00:05:09,288
Ram... Lakshman...

51
00:05:09,502 --> 00:05:11,379
...come here, my sons!

52
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:17,651
O sage Vishwamitra...

53
00:05:17,865 --> 00:05:19,741
...I leave my sons with you.

54
00:05:19,955 --> 00:05:21,832
Give them guidance and courage.

55
00:05:22,046 --> 00:05:23,922
Bless you, King Dashrath!

56
00:05:24,136 --> 00:05:28,105
You have made a decision
that shall save the world.

57
00:05:28,492 --> 00:05:31,236
We will obey you
like we obey our father.

58
00:05:31,453 --> 00:05:33,330
Your wishes will
be our command.

59
00:06:02,639 --> 00:06:04,694
You know, once this
was a beautiful forest...

60
00:06:04,903 --> 00:06:08,871
...but now it has dried up
because of a terrible cannibal...

61
00:06:09,084 --> 00:06:10,961
...a demoness called Tadaka.

62
00:06:11,175 --> 00:06:13,051
Her son, the evil Marich...

63
00:06:13,266 --> 00:06:15,142
...leads the demons...

64
00:06:15,356 --> 00:06:17,233
...who defile the holy fires.

65
00:06:17,447 --> 00:06:19,323
Ram, you must kill Tadaka.

66
00:06:19,537 --> 00:06:21,414
That is your dharma!

67
00:06:21,628 --> 00:06:23,504
Your duty as a Kshatriya!

68
00:06:24,590 --> 00:06:26,646
I shall teach you Mantras...

69
00:06:26,854 --> 00:06:28,731
They will guide you.

70
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:31,867
Now... repeat after me.

71
00:06:49,678 --> 00:06:51,733
Stop it!

72
00:06:53,859 --> 00:06:57,993
That mantra tears apart...

73
00:07:28,354 --> 00:07:31,454
Ram, use the mantra.
Recite the mantra!

74
00:08:15,566 --> 00:08:17,442
Many years ago...

75
00:08:17,656 --> 00:08:19,533
...in this very place...

76
00:08:20,619 --> 00:08:23,719
...the Gods rewarded
my long years of penance...

77
00:08:23,928 --> 00:08:26,850
...with the mastery
of supreme weapons.

78
00:08:28,109 --> 00:08:29,986
The time has now come...

79
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:32,076
...for me to pass
on these weapons...

80
00:08:32,291 --> 00:08:34,167
...to one worthy of them.

81
00:08:39,608 --> 00:08:42,530
Take them, Ram,
and use them well.

82
00:08:51,978 --> 00:08:54,033
They are now yours.

83
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:56,118
Use them to protect 'Dharma'.

84
00:09:15,148 --> 00:09:19,116
That's him!
The one who killed my mother.

85
00:09:19,329 --> 00:09:21,206
I shall avenge
her with his blood...

86
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:23,296
...this I swear!

87
00:09:26,473 --> 00:09:28,528
Watch out!

88
00:10:02,186 --> 00:10:04,063
You used the divine weapons!

89
00:10:04,277 --> 00:10:06,154
How did you learn so soon?

90
00:10:06,368 --> 00:10:08,244
These are the weapons of the Gods.

91
00:10:10,376 --> 00:10:13,476
And the righteous one needs
no lessons to use them.

92
00:10:14,730 --> 00:10:16,607
Show me, my Guru...

93
00:10:16,821 --> 00:10:18,697
...how to use this Chakra?

94
00:10:18,911 --> 00:10:21,833
You will learn but only
if you pursue your destiny...

95
00:10:22,047 --> 00:10:23,924
...in righteousness.

96
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:39,608
Listen all!

97
00:10:39,817 --> 00:10:42,739
This is the great bow of Shiva!

98
00:10:42,953 --> 00:10:44,830
He who lifts it and strings it...

99
00:10:45,916 --> 00:10:49,016
...shall receive a
great reward from King Janak.

100
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:52,147
The winner shall be given...

101
00:10:52,361 --> 00:10:54,237
...the hand of Princess Sita.

102
00:10:54,452 --> 00:10:56,328
...in marriage.

103
00:11:24,765 --> 00:11:27,687
Next, Prince Jagtara of Sorav.

104
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:51,208
Next, the Prince Ram of Ayodhya.

105
00:12:47,867 --> 00:12:50,789
Congratulations on
your wedding, Prince Ram.

106
00:13:09,819 --> 00:13:11,695
Years passed.

107
00:13:11,909 --> 00:13:13,786
Ayodhya grew and prospered.

108
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,876
And the people loved Ram.

109
00:13:16,961 --> 00:13:19,016
Their prince and king-to-be.

110
00:13:19,226 --> 00:13:21,103
The four brothers live in harmony...

111
00:13:21,317 --> 00:13:24,239
...and their future looks full of hope.

112
00:13:27,589 --> 00:13:30,510
My people, this morning I awoke
from a dream full of omens.

113
00:13:30,725 --> 00:13:32,601
Guru Vashishtha sees in them...

114
00:13:32,815 --> 00:13:34,692
...the coming of troubled times.

115
00:13:36,996 --> 00:13:38,873
But my health is failing...

116
00:13:39,087 --> 00:13:40,963
I am getting old and...

117
00:13:41,178 --> 00:13:43,054
...have no more power
to resist those evil forces.

118
00:13:44,139 --> 00:13:46,194
I have, therefore, decided...

119
00:13:46,404 --> 00:13:48,281
...that Ram will succeed me.

120
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:51,416
He will be the
next king of Ayodhya.

121
00:13:51,631 --> 00:13:54,552
Ram, my son, come forward.

122
00:13:59,993 --> 00:14:02,915
Ram, try to live up
to the people's expectations.

123
00:14:03,129 --> 00:14:05,005
I have faith in you.

124
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:07,096
I will do my utmost...

125
00:14:07,310 --> 00:14:09,187
...to live up to the
ideals you have set for us.

126
00:14:09,401 --> 00:14:11,277
Long live Ayodhya!

127
00:14:11,491 --> 00:14:13,368
Long live King Dashrath!

128
00:14:13,582 --> 00:14:15,458
Long live Prince Ram!

129
00:14:25,951 --> 00:14:28,006
Get away... get away.

130
00:14:28,216 --> 00:14:31,138
Noisy wretched things!

131
00:14:31,352 --> 00:14:33,229
Manthara, stop abusing the birds.

132
00:14:34,313 --> 00:14:36,369
Aah... Kekeyi, is this the time...

133
00:14:36,578 --> 00:14:38,455
...to beautify yourself?

134
00:14:38,669 --> 00:14:41,591
When great misfortune
creeps upon the kingdom?

135
00:14:41,805 --> 00:14:44,727
Manthara, don't you understand?

136
00:14:48,948 --> 00:14:51,003
Our beloved Ram is to be anointed...

137
00:14:51,213 --> 00:14:53,089
...crown prince tomorrow.

138
00:14:53,303 --> 00:14:56,225
And so I said,
it is a misfortune.

139
00:14:56,439 --> 00:14:59,361
Oh Kekeyi...

140
00:14:59,575 --> 00:15:01,452
...you are so innocent!

141
00:15:01,666 --> 00:15:03,542
So trusting! And look...

142
00:15:03,756 --> 00:15:07,724
...look how King Dashrath
has betrayed your trust!?

143
00:15:07,938 --> 00:15:09,814
Hold your tongue, Manthara.

144
00:15:10,028 --> 00:15:11,905
I will never allow you to
speak of the King in this way.

145
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:13,995
Why? Why do you think...

146
00:15:14,209 --> 00:15:17,131
...the king sent Bharat away, now?

147
00:15:17,345 --> 00:15:19,222
So conveniently...

148
00:15:19,436 --> 00:15:22,358
... before the coronation! Why!?

149
00:15:23,617 --> 00:15:26,539
Why? I wonder why he did that?

150
00:15:28,669 --> 00:15:31,770
Kaushalya might have suggested it...

151
00:15:31,979 --> 00:15:33,856
...to the king. Yes!

152
00:15:34,070 --> 00:15:36,992
You know you are the
king's favorite queen...

153
00:15:37,206 --> 00:15:40,128
...and Kaushalya hates you for that.

154
00:15:40,342 --> 00:15:42,218
She is jealous... jealous...

155
00:15:42,432 --> 00:15:45,354
...of your youth
and beauty, aah!

156
00:15:46,614 --> 00:15:48,490
What can I do?

157
00:15:48,704 --> 00:15:50,581
Leave everything...

158
00:15:50,795 --> 00:15:53,717
...to this loyal
and clever Manthara.

159
00:16:17,973 --> 00:16:19,849
What's happened?

160
00:16:21,109 --> 00:16:22,985
Why this sorrow, this anger...

161
00:16:23,199 --> 00:16:25,076
...on such an auspicious night?

162
00:16:25,290 --> 00:16:27,166
What can I do?
Come, tell me.

163
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:30,302
Tell me O King,
do you remember when you were...

164
00:16:30,516 --> 00:16:32,393
...injured in a
battle some years ago?

165
00:16:40,969 --> 00:16:42,846
I drove you to safety...

166
00:16:43,931 --> 00:16:48,065
...and you promised to
fulfill two boons of mine.

167
00:16:52,468 --> 00:16:54,344
You must grant me...

168
00:16:54,558 --> 00:16:56,435
...those two boons, now!

169
00:16:56,649 --> 00:16:58,525
Only two boons!?

170
00:17:00,656 --> 00:17:02,711
You can have more,
if you want.

171
00:17:02,921 --> 00:17:04,797
No, I don't need more than two.

172
00:17:05,882 --> 00:17:07,937
The first is...

173
00:17:10,063 --> 00:17:12,118
No... I cannot grant you...

174
00:17:12,328 --> 00:17:14,205
...those, Kekeyi. Not those!

175
00:17:14,419 --> 00:17:17,341
I will give you all my wealth.
Will that please you? - No.

176
00:17:19,471 --> 00:17:21,526
Do you wanted to be known...

177
00:17:21,736 --> 00:17:24,658
...that a king of Solar Dynasty
went back on his words.

178
00:17:24,872 --> 00:17:26,748
I will be content...

179
00:17:26,963 --> 00:17:29,884
...with only those two boons.

180
00:17:33,234 --> 00:17:35,111
The boons were...

181
00:17:36,196 --> 00:17:39,296
...one, Kekeyi's son,
Bharat, to be made king...

182
00:17:39,506 --> 00:17:42,428
...and two,
Ram to be banished...

183
00:17:42,642 --> 00:17:45,564
...to the forest
for fourteen years.

184
00:17:47,694 --> 00:17:49,749
Brother, can you not hear
the people's voices?

185
00:17:49,959 --> 00:17:52,881
Lakshman, this
is part of my fate.

186
00:17:53,095 --> 00:17:56,017
But are we, on that
account to sit still...

187
00:17:56,231 --> 00:17:58,108
...and do nothing?
This sword...

188
00:17:58,322 --> 00:18:00,198
...is it only an ornament,
just a plaything?

189
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:03,334
Brother, you are part
of my self, sharing...

190
00:18:03,548 --> 00:18:05,425
...the same soul with me.
Please...

191
00:18:06,510 --> 00:18:08,565
...try to understand me.

192
00:18:08,775 --> 00:18:10,651
My Lord, I am
coming with you.

193
00:18:12,433 --> 00:18:13,787
But Sita, you...

194
00:18:16,092 --> 00:18:19,014
A husband's duty
is his wife's too.

195
00:18:19,228 --> 00:18:21,104
Your fate is equally mine.
- That's right!

196
00:18:24,454 --> 00:18:26,331
And the same soul should
follow the same fate.

197
00:18:26,545 --> 00:18:29,467
And so brother, I, too,
am coming with you.

198
00:18:32,642 --> 00:18:34,697
Thank you!

199
00:18:45,186 --> 00:18:47,241
Mother... take heart!

200
00:18:47,451 --> 00:18:49,327
Fourteen years will
pass very quickly.

201
00:18:49,541 --> 00:18:53,510
And I will be back, seeking your
blessings in no time at all.

202
00:18:53,723 --> 00:18:55,599
Yes, my son. - Ram!

203
00:19:06,092 --> 00:19:09,192
Ram, why don't
you blame me?

204
00:19:09,402 --> 00:19:11,279
Why don't you bear
a grudge against me?

205
00:19:11,493 --> 00:19:13,369
That would ease my guilt.

206
00:19:14,454 --> 00:19:17,555
I don't want the kingdom.
Nor the power.

207
00:19:17,764 --> 00:19:21,733
All I want are your blessings
before we depart. Father!

208
00:19:23,862 --> 00:19:25,917
My son, bring glory to our
great line of kings.

209
00:19:26,127 --> 00:19:28,003
Come back safe.

210
00:19:31,353 --> 00:19:34,275
Who in the world can
boast of a son like you?

211
00:19:38,670 --> 00:19:40,547
Sumantra...

212
00:19:42,852 --> 00:19:45,774
...get ready the chariots,
the elephants, horses and...

213
00:19:45,988 --> 00:19:47,864
...foot soldiers to accompany
Ram to the forest.

214
00:19:48,078 --> 00:19:49,955
Yes, your majesty!

215
00:19:50,169 --> 00:19:53,091
Father, when nature herself
will take care of me...

216
00:19:53,305 --> 00:19:56,227
...what use I have of an army,
of royal pageantry?

217
00:19:56,441 --> 00:19:59,362
Of course, you will
give Bharat this kingdom...

218
00:19:59,577 --> 00:20:02,498
...after draining it
of all its wealth.

219
00:20:22,573 --> 00:20:25,495
Mother, give your blessings
to your departing son.

220
00:20:35,988 --> 00:20:38,043
Ram, don't leave us.

221
00:20:38,253 --> 00:20:41,174
Remain as our king.
- Beloved citizens...

222
00:20:42,259 --> 00:20:44,315
You know how
much I love you.

223
00:20:44,524 --> 00:20:46,401
And I know how much
you love me.

224
00:20:46,615 --> 00:20:48,492
You will show your
love for me by...

225
00:20:48,706 --> 00:20:50,582
...loving my noble brother, Bharat...

226
00:20:50,796 --> 00:20:53,718
...who is fully worthy of your
love and of being your king.

227
00:20:54,977 --> 00:20:57,899
Support him, I beg of you. Support...

228
00:20:58,984 --> 00:21:02,085
...my sorrowful father. People
of Ayodhya, I appeal to you.

229
00:21:03,165 --> 00:21:06,266
Rama... don't go, Rama, Please.

230
00:21:24,071 --> 00:21:26,127
Ram... come back soon!

231
00:21:32,608 --> 00:21:34,485
O my son!

232
00:21:35,744 --> 00:21:37,621
Ram!

233
00:21:38,776 --> 00:21:39,713
Take care...

234
00:21:39,925 --> 00:21:42,847
...Ram, Lakshman, Sita!

235
00:21:43,061 --> 00:21:44,938
You take care too.

236
00:21:45,152 --> 00:21:48,074
And please, look after my father.

237
00:21:48,288 --> 00:21:50,164
I will.

238
00:22:41,424 --> 00:22:43,479
RAM!!!

239
00:23:01,354 --> 00:23:03,339
Six months passed by.

240
00:23:03,549 --> 00:23:05,426
King Dashrath's palace is...

241
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:07,517
...enveloped in darkness.

242
00:23:07,731 --> 00:23:09,607
Ram...

243
00:23:10,692 --> 00:23:12,747
...forgive your father.

244
00:23:12,957 --> 00:23:14,834
Ram... Ram!

245
00:23:20,274 --> 00:23:24,242
He is free from the
sufferings of this world.

246
00:23:29,508 --> 00:23:31,563
Bharat, Kekeyi's son...

247
00:23:31,773 --> 00:23:33,649
...who was away in Kekeya...

248
00:23:33,863 --> 00:23:35,740
...visiting his grandfather...

249
00:23:35,954 --> 00:23:38,876
...was called back to Ayodhya.

250
00:24:06,093 --> 00:24:08,148
Mother... mother! What is this?
What has happened?

251
00:24:09,229 --> 00:24:12,329
Oh Bharat, you have come at last.

252
00:24:12,539 --> 00:24:16,508
Tell me mother, is it true,
father has passed away?

253
00:24:17,591 --> 00:24:19,647
Oh God!

254
00:24:20,727 --> 00:24:22,782
Then it is true! - Yes.

255
00:24:22,992 --> 00:24:25,914
But he left us a great honor.
- What is it?

256
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:35,322
What have you done,
you depraved heartless woman?

257
00:24:37,627 --> 00:24:40,548
What perverse tongue
poisoned your mind?

258
00:24:40,762 --> 00:24:42,639
Brother, it is she.

259
00:24:42,853 --> 00:24:45,775
It is this evil wretch
who has sown the...

260
00:24:45,989 --> 00:24:48,911
...seed of madness
in our mother's heart.

261
00:24:49,125 --> 00:24:51,001
Please...

262
00:24:51,215 --> 00:24:53,092
...please forgive me.

263
00:24:54,177 --> 00:24:57,277
I was only thinking of you two...

264
00:24:57,487 --> 00:25:00,409
...Kekeyi and Bharat's...
- Stop it.

265
00:25:00,623 --> 00:25:04,591
I will cleave your filthy
brain in two. - That's enough.

266
00:25:04,804 --> 00:25:07,726
Don't let her blood
defile our father's soul.

267
00:25:08,986 --> 00:25:11,907
You are no longer my mother...

268
00:25:12,122 --> 00:25:13,998
...let the world know it.

269
00:25:15,083 --> 00:25:17,138
Please forgive me...

270
00:25:17,348 --> 00:25:20,270
...forgive your
poor mother, Bharat...

271
00:25:20,484 --> 00:25:23,406
...please, forgive me.

272
00:25:25,536 --> 00:25:27,591
Forgive me!

273
00:25:36,059 --> 00:25:36,997
What?

274
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:40,135
What are you saying, Bharat?

275
00:25:40,345 --> 00:25:43,266
Our father is dead!?

276
00:25:43,481 --> 00:25:45,357
Brother...

277
00:25:45,571 --> 00:25:47,448
...I share your grief.

278
00:25:54,979 --> 00:25:56,855
Father... father...

279
00:25:57,940 --> 00:25:59,995
...forgive this poor Ram...

280
00:26:00,205 --> 00:26:02,082
...forgive your son, please.

281
00:26:03,341 --> 00:26:05,218
Ram, I appeal to you...

282
00:26:05,432 --> 00:26:07,308
...absolve me of my mother's sin.

283
00:26:07,522 --> 00:26:11,491
Come back to Ayodhya and accept...

284
00:26:11,704 --> 00:26:13,580
...the kingdom which is
yours by right. - Bharat...

285
00:26:13,794 --> 00:26:15,671
...what your mother has done
is not in question here.

286
00:26:15,885 --> 00:26:19,853
Remember, the great Emperor
Dashrath has commanded us...

287
00:26:20,937 --> 00:26:24,037
...you to rule the kingdom and I...

288
00:26:24,247 --> 00:26:26,124
...to live in this forest
for fourteen years.

289
00:26:26,338 --> 00:26:29,260
It is our duty to abide
by our father's wishes...

290
00:26:29,474 --> 00:26:31,350
...whether we like it or not.

291
00:26:31,564 --> 00:26:33,441
You have commanded me,
it is enough.

292
00:26:33,655 --> 00:26:35,532
But one thing is certain.

293
00:26:35,746 --> 00:26:38,667
I will not accept
the kingdom for myself.

294
00:26:38,881 --> 00:26:40,758
But for you!

295
00:26:44,108 --> 00:26:46,003
Please bless this
brother of yours...

296
00:26:46,218 --> 00:26:49,157
...to rule the kingdom with
strength and courage.

297
00:26:59,885 --> 00:27:01,773
I will rule for the
next fourteen years...

298
00:27:01,988 --> 00:27:03,875
...but only till you return.

299
00:27:04,090 --> 00:27:07,555
Bharat, my brother. - Ram.

300
00:27:07,770 --> 00:27:09,836
Long live Ram.

301
00:27:10,048 --> 00:27:12,281
Long live Bharat.

302
00:28:17,506 --> 00:28:19,573
What brings my
chief minister out here...

303
00:28:19,784 --> 00:28:21,672
...at this unlikely hour?

304
00:28:21,887 --> 00:28:24,826
Sir, in the forest of
Dandaka and Janasthana...

305
00:28:25,041 --> 00:28:27,980
...they say the holy men are
returning to their ashrams.

306
00:28:28,195 --> 00:28:30,082
They seem to have
gained a new confidence.

307
00:28:30,297 --> 00:28:33,236
Our spies say, it is
the doing of the young...

308
00:28:33,451 --> 00:28:35,339
...prince of Ayodhya,
Prince Ram.

309
00:28:37,481 --> 00:28:41,639
Oh, this boy Ram is
handsome, isn't he?

310
00:28:42,738 --> 00:28:44,805
I've heard this
Ram is a cowards...

311
00:28:45,016 --> 00:28:47,954
...who has been sent into
exile by his own people.

312
00:28:48,170 --> 00:28:50,057
That's right,
my king, but we must...

313
00:28:50,272 --> 00:28:52,160
...do something before
it is too late.

314
00:28:53,426 --> 00:28:57,417
Oh Ram, I can't
wait to see you.

315
00:31:39,708 --> 00:31:41,595
Shurpankha, Ravan's
younger sister...

316
00:31:41,810 --> 00:31:45,801
.disguised as a beautiful
lady comes to Panchvati...

317
00:31:46,015 --> 00:31:47,903
...to entice Ram.

318
00:31:49,169 --> 00:31:52,108
I am Shurpankha.

319
00:31:57,404 --> 00:31:59,471
Ram, you are so beautiful...

320
00:32:00,558 --> 00:32:02,625
...strong and handsome.

321
00:32:02,836 --> 00:32:04,724
I have decided to marry you.

322
00:32:07,041 --> 00:32:08,929
Your wish would be my command...

323
00:32:09,144 --> 00:32:11,031
...were it not for my
wife Sita, there.

324
00:32:11,247 --> 00:32:14,185
Why don't you approach
my brother, Lakshman?

325
00:32:14,401 --> 00:32:17,339
He is also very handsome
and very strong.

326
00:32:17,555 --> 00:32:20,493
Hmm... he is handsome too.

327
00:32:20,708 --> 00:32:23,647
I speak with your interest at
heart. I am only second to Ram.

328
00:32:23,862 --> 00:32:27,853
And I don't think you are the
kind to settle for second best!?

329
00:32:28,068 --> 00:32:29,955
Yes, you are right!

330
00:32:31,046 --> 00:32:34,164
I am the kind to settle only
for the very best.

331
00:32:35,251 --> 00:32:39,409
Come... come. I will introduce
you to... this is my wife Sita.

332
00:32:45,940 --> 00:32:52,033
This ugly one is your
wife!? I will kill her.

333
00:32:58,555 --> 00:33:00,443
Oh... my nose.

334
00:33:01,709 --> 00:33:03,597
My nose!!

335
00:33:04,688 --> 00:33:06,755
Bleeding!

336
00:33:08,893 --> 00:33:12,011
O the Energy which bestows
knowledge to conquer...

337
00:33:12,222 --> 00:33:15,161
...the phenomenon of death...
may please rise... rise...

338
00:33:15,376 --> 00:33:19,367
...and bestow your
blessings! Swaha!

339
00:33:22,560 --> 00:33:24,627
Brother! - What's
happened to you?

340
00:33:24,838 --> 00:33:27,777
O our little sister!
What has happened!?

341
00:33:30,970 --> 00:33:34,089
Ram!? You mean that... that...
prince from Ayodhya!?

342
00:33:34,300 --> 00:33:37,238
Is he the one
who attacked you?

343
00:33:52,172 --> 00:33:54,059
Do not worry, little sister.

344
00:33:54,274 --> 00:33:57,213
I will have these
worms sliced up and...

345
00:33:57,428 --> 00:33:59,316
...and feed the
ravens for breakfast.

346
00:33:59,531 --> 00:34:01,418
Where is my brother Kumbhakarna?

347
00:34:01,634 --> 00:34:04,572
Tell him, I have said, he
must lead the attack.

348
00:34:26,865 --> 00:34:28,752
Just as I feared, my King...

349
00:34:28,968 --> 00:34:31,906
...your brother Kumbhakarna won't
wake up for the next six months.

350
00:34:32,121 --> 00:34:36,112
That Sita... I wish I
could destroy her beauty.

351
00:34:37,203 --> 00:34:39,269
Is she... that beautiful?

352
00:34:40,356 --> 00:34:44,514
There is no one more beautiful
than her in this whole world.

353
00:34:47,891 --> 00:34:51,882
Her waist is slim,
her figure captivating...

354
00:34:52,096 --> 00:34:56,087
...her complexion
like molten gold.

355
00:34:58,404 --> 00:35:03,446
A heavenly maid who is
designed for you, my brother.

356
00:35:03,661 --> 00:35:05,548
She is not worthy of that Ram.

357
00:35:06,814 --> 00:35:09,753
There surely is someone
who is worthy of her.

358
00:35:09,968 --> 00:35:12,907
And that someone is you.

359
00:35:45,537 --> 00:35:48,656
Ravan, accompanied by
his uncle Marich...

360
00:35:48,867 --> 00:35:50,754
...sets out to kidnap Sita.

361
00:35:52,021 --> 00:35:54,959
Then... as we planned?

362
00:35:55,174 --> 00:35:59,165
Yes, as we planned!

363
00:36:04,461 --> 00:36:06,528
This is magnificent!!!

364
00:36:07,615 --> 00:36:10,733
And this can
surely deceive Ram.

365
00:36:23,384 --> 00:36:25,451
Oh... how beautiful she is!

366
00:36:31,970 --> 00:36:34,909
Oh! How lovely!

367
00:36:35,124 --> 00:36:38,063
It 'is' real, isn't it?
It's not a dream, is it?

368
00:36:38,278 --> 00:36:41,217
O Ram, won't you
capture the deer for me?

369
00:36:41,432 --> 00:36:44,370
It is the most beautiful
thing I've ever seen.

370
00:36:44,586 --> 00:36:47,524
For you? I will!
Lakshman, look after Sita.

371
00:36:55,099 --> 00:36:58,037
Brother, remember that this
deer's beauty is Shurpankha.

372
00:36:58,253 --> 00:37:01,191
Watch out! Watch out for
those treacherous creatures.

373
00:37:01,407 --> 00:37:03,294
All right! Protect Sita.

374
00:37:14,022 --> 00:37:16,961
So, it is a demon,
disguised as a deer!

375
00:37:26,638 --> 00:37:30,629
You might be relieved
that you have killed me.

376
00:37:30,843 --> 00:37:33,782
But you better be worried
about your pretty wife.

377
00:37:33,997 --> 00:37:36,936
What? - Lakshman, Sita...

378
00:37:37,151 --> 00:37:39,038
...help me!

379
00:37:41,356 --> 00:37:44,295
Lakshman, did you hear
that dreadful cry?

380
00:37:44,510 --> 00:37:47,449
Ram is in danger.
He needs your help.

381
00:37:47,664 --> 00:37:50,603
O he will be safe.
Don't worry, sister.

382
00:37:50,818 --> 00:37:53,757
What are you saying?
You wish him dead?

383
00:37:55,023 --> 00:37:57,962
I understand, so,
I will obey you!

384
00:38:10,793 --> 00:38:13,731
Sister, do not step
outside this line.

385
00:38:13,947 --> 00:38:16,885
Within this line you
are safe. I assure you.

386
00:38:25,511 --> 00:38:29,502
Everything goes
just as I planned.

387
00:38:53,721 --> 00:38:56,839
Om Namah Shivay!
(Obeisance to Lord Shiva!)

388
00:38:59,153 --> 00:39:01,040
O virtuous lady...

389
00:39:02,131 --> 00:39:04,198
...I come begging for alms.

390
00:39:20,179 --> 00:39:22,066
Here you are.

391
00:39:25,435 --> 00:39:27,323
Oh, I am surprised.

392
00:39:27,538 --> 00:39:30,477
Somebody has drawn it
to protect you.

393
00:39:30,692 --> 00:39:33,630
I cannot cross it but
you surely can. Come.

394
00:39:34,722 --> 00:39:36,789
No... no.

395
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:40,991
If you do not feed this hungry
saint with your hands...

396
00:39:41,205 --> 00:39:46,247
...then ruin shall fall upon
your father's and father-in-law's house...

397
00:39:46,461 --> 00:39:48,349
...O noble lady!

398
00:40:16,774 --> 00:40:19,892
Lakshman!? - Ram! - Why did
you leave Sita alone?

399
00:40:20,103 --> 00:40:23,042
Why are you here? - She
insisted I leave when we heard your cry.

400
00:40:23,257 --> 00:40:27,248
Oh no! That was the voice of
demon imitating mine.

401
00:40:27,462 --> 00:40:29,350
I fear the worst. Come...

402
00:40:29,565 --> 00:40:31,452
...let's get back
as soon as we can.

403
00:40:33,595 --> 00:40:35,662
Ram... Ram!

404
00:40:41,129 --> 00:40:43,017
Rescue me!

405
00:40:47,262 --> 00:40:50,380
Lakshman... Ram... help me!

406
00:40:51,467 --> 00:40:52,482
Sita!

407
00:40:53,745 --> 00:40:58,787
You are mine now. - No... no...
Jatayu, help me. No!!

408
00:41:07,412 --> 00:41:10,350
Let her go. She does
not belong to you.

409
00:41:20,027 --> 00:41:21,915
Let me go. Oh!

410
00:41:28,438 --> 00:41:30,325
Jatayu...

411
00:41:39,827 --> 00:41:40,842
Will teach him a lesson.

412
00:41:44,032 --> 00:41:46,099
Jatayu...

413
00:41:49,464 --> 00:41:51,351
Let me go.

414
00:41:51,567 --> 00:41:54,505
No one can save you now.

415
00:42:08,212 --> 00:42:10,279
He tricked me!

416
00:42:10,490 --> 00:42:13,429
He tricked me and abducted my
wife during my absence.

417
00:42:15,747 --> 00:42:18,685
I swear, Lakshman, I swear.
I shall try to vanquish him.

418
00:42:19,776 --> 00:42:22,895
I shall follow that fellow
into the ends of the universe.

419
00:42:23,106 --> 00:42:24,993
I will seek him out.

420
00:42:25,208 --> 00:42:28,147
And I... will destroy him.

421
00:42:30,465 --> 00:42:33,403
Calm down, my brother Ram.
You have always said that...

422
00:42:33,619 --> 00:42:36,557
...anger is not the right
path to justice.

423
00:42:36,773 --> 00:42:39,711
You, who have only the good
of the world at heart...

424
00:42:39,927 --> 00:42:42,865
...must not let anger
plunge you into it.

425
00:42:45,008 --> 00:42:47,075
You are right...
you are right, Lakshman.

426
00:42:48,162 --> 00:42:51,280
Now, it is your turn to lead...

427
00:42:51,491 --> 00:42:54,430
...my little brother
and I will follow.

428
00:42:55,521 --> 00:42:57,588
Lakshman, is this
gentle creature...

429
00:42:57,799 --> 00:42:59,686
...trying to tell us
something about Sita?

430
00:42:59,901 --> 00:43:02,840
It might be showing us
the direction...

431
00:43:03,055 --> 00:43:04,943
...in which Sita has been
taken. Let's go.

432
00:43:05,158 --> 00:43:09,149
Help me! Ram... Ram!!!

433
00:43:13,568 --> 00:43:15,456
Hey, what is this?

434
00:43:18,825 --> 00:43:20,712
Forgive me, Ram...

435
00:43:20,927 --> 00:43:23,866
...I tried to stop him,
but he cantered away.

436
00:43:24,081 --> 00:43:27,020
My old wings were too frail.

437
00:43:27,235 --> 00:43:30,174
Oh Jatayu...

438
00:43:30,389 --> 00:43:32,276
...how can I blame you?

439
00:43:33,368 --> 00:43:36,486
You have given your life's
blood for my beloved wife!

440
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:40,855
Do not lose heart, Ram.
You will find her again.

441
00:43:41,057 --> 00:43:43,831
Jatayu... Jatayu...

442
00:43:49,988 --> 00:43:51,769
Where are you taking me?

443
00:43:52,799 --> 00:43:54,750
Let me go.

444
00:44:08,841 --> 00:44:11,615
Remember all of you. If anyone
tries to harm her...

445
00:44:11,818 --> 00:44:14,592
...they will die. This lady
here is so noble...

446
00:44:14,795 --> 00:44:17,569
...that even looking at you
makes her impure.

447
00:44:18,599 --> 00:44:20,550
Trijata!? - What does Your Majesty wish of me?

448
00:44:20,749 --> 00:44:22,530
I appoint you her keeper.

449
00:44:22,734 --> 00:44:24,515
Whatever she asks for
in the Ashok Van...

450
00:44:25,545 --> 00:44:27,496
...see that she gets it.
- Very well, your Majesty.

451
00:44:27,695 --> 00:44:31,462
She is stubborn. But you must
give her everything she wants.

452
00:44:31,664 --> 00:44:33,446
Except freedom!

453
00:44:49,426 --> 00:44:51,310
Could it be...

454
00:44:51,510 --> 00:44:55,277
...human blood? Yum... yum... yum.

455
00:44:55,479 --> 00:44:57,261
So good!

456
00:45:00,275 --> 00:45:02,226
An arrow!? Painful
if it hits me.

457
00:45:04,244 --> 00:45:06,195
But it doesn't hit me.

458
00:45:11,190 --> 00:45:13,141
I got her!

459
00:45:45,094 --> 00:45:49,853
Thank you! I was a heavenly
creature, cursed to be...

460
00:45:50,055 --> 00:45:52,829
...an ugly demon. And no one
could lift the curse.

461
00:45:53,032 --> 00:45:55,806
Only if I were defeated by
a man of justice...

462
00:45:56,009 --> 00:45:59,776
...I could regain my original
self and go back to the heavens.

463
00:46:00,805 --> 00:46:02,756
Thank you, Ram. But...

464
00:46:02,955 --> 00:46:04,736
...there is nothing I can do
for you in return, except...

465
00:46:04,940 --> 00:46:07,713
...give you advice.

466
00:46:07,917 --> 00:46:10,690
Find Sugriva now.

467
00:46:11,720 --> 00:46:13,671
Sugriva!? Who is he?

468
00:46:18,832 --> 00:46:20,613
It's a lake.

469
00:46:21,643 --> 00:46:23,594
Lakshman, now what do we do?

470
00:46:23,793 --> 00:46:26,567
There seems to be someone over
there. Let's go and...

471
00:46:26,770 --> 00:46:28,551
...ask them about Sugriva.
- That's a good idea.

472
00:46:32,724 --> 00:46:34,505
Wait!

473
00:46:44,631 --> 00:46:47,405
And in the great
mother's magic play...

474
00:46:47,608 --> 00:46:50,382
...all of us perform
our little roles.

475
00:46:52,570 --> 00:46:56,337
I never thought I could see a
man of knowledge like you...

476
00:46:56,539 --> 00:46:59,313
...in this wilderness. My name
is Ram and this is my brother Lakshman.

477
00:46:59,516 --> 00:47:01,297
We are the sons of
King Dashrath of Ayodhya.

478
00:47:01,500 --> 00:47:05,267
We come in search of my
beloved wife, Sita...

479
00:47:05,470 --> 00:47:07,251
...who has been carried
away by a demon...

480
00:47:07,454 --> 00:47:09,235
...I know not, where?

481
00:47:09,439 --> 00:47:12,212
Indeed it is a benevolent
destiny that leads me...

482
00:47:12,416 --> 00:47:14,197
...to Prince Ram of Ayodhya.

483
00:47:16,219 --> 00:47:19,162
My name is Hanuman.

484
00:47:19,362 --> 00:47:22,135
And I am minister to
the King Sugriva.

485
00:47:22,338 --> 00:47:26,105
Lakshman, we've been wondering
where to find Sugriva...

486
00:47:26,308 --> 00:47:29,081
...and here is Sugriva's
messenger welcoming us.

487
00:47:29,285 --> 00:47:32,058
Indeed kind destiny
has guided us here.

488
00:47:33,088 --> 00:47:35,039
Ram... Lakshman...

489
00:47:35,238 --> 00:47:38,012
...it is indeed an honor to meet
the sons of King Dashrath...

490
00:47:38,215 --> 00:47:40,989
...whose greatness is known in
all four corners of the world.

491
00:47:41,192 --> 00:47:44,959
Under strange circumstances I
heard your name called out...

492
00:47:45,161 --> 00:47:46,943
...Ram!

493
00:47:47,146 --> 00:47:49,919
Not many days ago, a flying
chariot, swift as a wind...

494
00:47:50,123 --> 00:47:51,904
...raced above our heads
and we heard...

495
00:47:52,107 --> 00:47:54,881
...and we heard a lady's
cry for help...

496
00:47:55,084 --> 00:47:57,858
Ram... she cried. Help me Ram!

497
00:47:58,061 --> 00:48:00,835
From the chariot, a small
bundle dropped to the ground.

498
00:48:01,038 --> 00:48:04,805
We've kept it very carefully.
- Where is it? Where is it?

499
00:48:07,984 --> 00:48:10,758
Oh brother, look...

500
00:48:10,961 --> 00:48:13,734
...indeed they are her scarf...

501
00:48:13,938 --> 00:48:15,719
...and the ornaments
in her hair.

502
00:48:15,922 --> 00:48:19,689
Oh Sita... my Sita.

503
00:48:19,891 --> 00:48:23,658
Courage brother, Ram.

504
00:48:23,861 --> 00:48:25,642
You have no time to grieve.
You must act without delay.

505
00:48:25,845 --> 00:48:29,612
I have sworn to rescue Sita
wherever she may be.

506
00:48:30,641 --> 00:48:33,584
Hmm, do well I know
how it hurts...

507
00:48:33,784 --> 00:48:35,565
...to be without one's consort.

508
00:48:35,768 --> 00:48:38,542
My brother Bali, banished
me from my kingdom...

509
00:48:38,745 --> 00:48:40,526
...then used up my wife.

510
00:48:40,730 --> 00:48:44,497
Oh, if only I had the kingdom's
army at my disposal...

511
00:48:44,699 --> 00:48:46,480
...I would send my men to search
the whole world...

512
00:48:46,683 --> 00:48:49,457
...to rescue your wife, Sita.

513
00:48:49,660 --> 00:48:52,434
Look, let us make this
government, O Prince of Ayodhya...

514
00:48:52,637 --> 00:48:55,411
Let us forge our strength in
friendship and swear to relieve...

515
00:48:55,614 --> 00:48:58,388
...the sorrows that have
befallen us both. - Yes, let us.

516
00:48:59,418 --> 00:49:01,369
For the sake of a friend...

517
00:49:01,568 --> 00:49:05,335
...a man should be ready to
give up his wealth...

518
00:49:05,537 --> 00:49:08,311
...and comforts and if
need be life itself.

519
00:49:08,514 --> 00:49:11,287
I will live by this Dharm and...

520
00:49:11,491 --> 00:49:13,272
...help Ram in every way.

521
00:49:13,475 --> 00:49:16,249
I swear it. - I swear it too.

522
00:49:17,444 --> 00:49:21,211
Ram fulfilled the promise given
to Sugriva and forked the mighty Bali.

523
00:49:22,406 --> 00:49:26,173
Bali was defeated and Sugriva
regained his wife and his kingdom.

524
00:49:26,375 --> 00:49:29,149
The monsoon clouds gathered
like a herd of elephants...

525
00:49:29,352 --> 00:49:32,126
...and reclaimed the Rishyamukha
hills for many days.

526
00:49:40,267 --> 00:49:43,041
And when the rain ceased and
the sun shone again Rishyamukha...

527
00:49:43,244 --> 00:49:47,011
...stood like an island.
surrounded by the waters of the flood.

528
00:49:50,190 --> 00:49:52,964
And Sugriva called forth his
great army of monkeys.

529
00:49:53,167 --> 00:49:54,948
When you find my Sita, give
her these ornaments...

530
00:49:55,152 --> 00:49:57,925
...so she may recognize you
as my emissaries.

531
00:50:17,974 --> 00:50:21,741
These are the jewels of my
clan. Please give them to her.

532
00:50:31,701 --> 00:50:34,644
The vanara king Sugriva sent
search parties in all directions...

533
00:50:34,843 --> 00:50:36,625
...keeping his promise to Ram.

534
00:50:57,666 --> 00:50:59,447
Help... it's a tiger. Help!

535
00:51:13,377 --> 00:51:15,328
Look... look... over there.

536
00:51:15,527 --> 00:51:18,301
If a bird came out of that cave, there
might be some water inside.

537
00:51:18,504 --> 00:51:21,278
Yes, perhaps we will
find some water there.

538
00:51:42,154 --> 00:51:44,104
They have gone inside.
- Gone inside now.

539
00:52:01,173 --> 00:52:02,954
Hey, I can see some light.

540
00:52:05,142 --> 00:52:06,923
That must be the way out. C'mon.

541
00:52:12,088 --> 00:52:14,862
Hanuman, who leads the
party to the south...

542
00:52:15,065 --> 00:52:16,846
...meets Sampaati...

543
00:52:17,049 --> 00:52:19,823
...brother of Jatayu...

544
00:52:20,026 --> 00:52:22,800
...the bird king, killed at
the hands of Ravan.

545
00:52:23,003 --> 00:52:24,785
Where are we?

546
00:52:31,934 --> 00:52:36,693
Are you not Jatayu's
brother, Sampaati!?

547
00:52:41,857 --> 00:52:45,624
Yes, I am Sampaati.

548
00:52:45,826 --> 00:52:48,600
Do you know my brother?

549
00:52:48,803 --> 00:52:51,576
How is my Jatayu?

550
00:52:52,606 --> 00:52:54,557
Is he well?

551
00:52:54,757 --> 00:52:57,530
Jatayu has found a
home in the heavens.

552
00:53:02,695 --> 00:53:04,476
Oh... how sad!

553
00:53:05,506 --> 00:53:07,457
How sad!

554
00:53:08,483 --> 00:53:11,426
My brother to die...

555
00:53:12,618 --> 00:53:16,385
...and I live on.

556
00:53:16,587 --> 00:53:19,361
Old though he was...

557
00:53:19,564 --> 00:53:23,331
...he fought a difficult battle
with an evil demon, Ravan...

558
00:53:24,360 --> 00:53:27,303
...and was slain as he
tried to save...

559
00:53:27,502 --> 00:53:31,269
...Mother Sita from
the demon's clutches?

560
00:53:31,471 --> 00:53:35,238
You said Ravan!?
Ravan is the name!?

561
00:53:35,441 --> 00:53:38,214
If I knew he had
killed my brother...

562
00:53:38,417 --> 00:53:41,191
...I would never have let him...

563
00:53:41,394 --> 00:53:43,176
...fly over this land, unharmed.

564
00:53:44,206 --> 00:53:46,156
He flew over here?

565
00:53:46,356 --> 00:53:48,137
Yes, look...

566
00:53:49,167 --> 00:53:51,118
...across the sea...

567
00:53:51,317 --> 00:53:54,091
...is Lanka.

568
00:53:55,121 --> 00:53:58,064
There you will find...

569
00:53:59,090 --> 00:54:03,015
...and his captive the lady.

570
00:54:03,225 --> 00:54:05,998
If we cross the sea
with all the troops...

571
00:54:06,202 --> 00:54:07,983
...we will need
thousands of boats.

572
00:54:09,013 --> 00:54:11,956
And I am too old now.

573
00:54:12,155 --> 00:54:15,922
Though in my youth I had
circled the earth 21 times.

574
00:54:18,936 --> 00:54:20,887
Now, there is only
one among us...

575
00:54:21,086 --> 00:54:22,867
...who can handle this task.

576
00:54:23,897 --> 00:54:25,848
When you were a boy...

577
00:54:26,047 --> 00:54:28,821
...believing the new born sun
to be a golden fruit...

578
00:54:29,024 --> 00:54:31,798
...you once flew after it...

579
00:54:32,001 --> 00:54:33,783
...meaning to swallow it up.

580
00:54:33,986 --> 00:54:35,767
You had great powers...

581
00:54:35,970 --> 00:54:39,737
...but you did not
know how to use them.

582
00:54:40,766 --> 00:54:43,709
The world was afraid of you...

583
00:54:43,743 --> 00:54:46,686
...and so you were put
under a spell...

584
00:54:46,886 --> 00:54:48,667
...that sealed your powers.

585
00:54:48,870 --> 00:54:51,644
But the time has not
come for me...

586
00:54:51,847 --> 00:54:53,628
...to unseal these
hidden powers.

587
00:54:54,658 --> 00:54:58,583
Only you can cross the sea
with your divine powers.

588
00:54:58,793 --> 00:55:02,560
Only you can reach Lanka
and find mother Sita.

589
00:55:46,258 --> 00:55:48,208
I... can fly!

590
00:55:54,196 --> 00:55:57,139
He has done it... he has done
it! How wonderful!

591
00:56:01,308 --> 00:56:05,074
Farewell prince!

592
00:56:12,057 --> 00:56:14,008
Hanuman rushes towards Lanka...

593
00:56:14,207 --> 00:56:16,981
...but is challenged by the
sea monster Sindhika.

594
00:56:18,011 --> 00:56:19,962
What's that?

595
00:56:55,718 --> 00:56:57,669
Where am I?

596
00:56:58,861 --> 00:57:00,642
I must get out of here.

597
00:57:19,699 --> 00:57:23,466
Now I will cut you up
to little pieces.

598
00:57:24,495 --> 00:57:28,419
After a furious battle Hanuman
tears the monster to pieces...

599
00:57:28,629 --> 00:57:31,403
...and proceeds towards the
island of Lanka.

600
00:59:23,570 --> 00:59:26,513
But on earth do I find Sita?

601
01:00:01,442 --> 01:00:03,224
Ah... you are awake.

602
01:00:04,254 --> 01:00:08,178
My day begins only when I see
the radiance of your face.

603
01:00:08,388 --> 01:00:11,162
And were you... you won't
even look at me.

604
01:00:11,365 --> 01:00:13,147
Do you not see I am starving
for your love?

605
01:00:14,342 --> 01:00:17,116
Perhaps I should make a
gift of Ram's head.

606
01:00:17,319 --> 01:00:19,100
So, you have visited
her again.

607
01:00:19,304 --> 01:00:21,085
Leave her alone, my Lord.

608
01:00:21,288 --> 01:00:24,062
Let's sing and dance over
there. Let's make merry.

609
01:00:27,076 --> 01:00:30,020
There is only a little time left.
The promise, dear, will soon be over.

610
01:00:37,165 --> 01:00:39,939
Huh! How on earth is our
lord attracted by you?

611
01:00:40,142 --> 01:00:42,915
I wonder what he sees in you!?

612
01:00:43,119 --> 01:00:45,892
I would like to see your husband.
I can't imagine anyone...

613
01:00:46,096 --> 01:00:48,869
...more handsome than the
Lord of Lanka.

614
01:00:49,072 --> 01:00:50,854
Go away all of you.
Do not annoy Sita...

615
01:00:51,057 --> 01:00:52,838
...or I will have to
answer to Ravan.

616
01:01:02,965 --> 01:01:05,738
O Ram! Ram, my husband...

617
01:01:06,768 --> 01:01:08,719
...come to save me quickly.

618
01:01:09,745 --> 01:01:11,696
O Ram!

619
01:01:12,722 --> 01:01:16,646
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

620
01:01:17,683 --> 01:01:21,608
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

621
01:01:22,645 --> 01:01:27,562
I bow at your feet...

622
01:01:27,772 --> 01:01:31,539
...having this great
opportunity with me.

623
01:01:31,741 --> 01:01:35,508
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

624
01:01:35,710 --> 01:01:40,469
O mother, I am
Ram's emissary.

625
01:01:51,421 --> 01:01:55,346
The radiance of my Lord is
like the shining sun...

626
01:01:56,383 --> 01:02:00,307
...and his voice is as soothing
as the moonlight.

627
01:02:01,344 --> 01:02:05,269
You have been
abducted by Ravan...

628
01:02:05,479 --> 01:02:08,253
...and he has called for his
own death by doing so.

629
01:02:08,456 --> 01:02:13,215
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

630
01:02:13,417 --> 01:02:18,177
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

631
01:02:29,128 --> 01:02:33,053
My Lord remains deep in
thought, each moment.

632
01:02:33,263 --> 01:02:37,030
But he constantly
thinks about you only.

633
01:02:38,059 --> 01:02:41,984
His eyes are always longing...

634
01:02:42,194 --> 01:02:44,967
...to see you, that's
my own knowledge.

635
01:02:45,171 --> 01:02:49,930
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

636
01:02:50,132 --> 01:02:54,891
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

637
01:03:06,009 --> 01:03:09,776
Come with me, mother.
I will take you back to Ram.

638
01:03:09,978 --> 01:03:12,752
I can't go with you. There
are many people in Lanka...

639
01:03:12,955 --> 01:03:15,729
...who have been abducted
and enslaved by force.

640
01:03:15,932 --> 01:03:18,705
I'm not the only one who
is to be rescued.

641
01:03:19,735 --> 01:03:21,686
Hmm... I understand.
I am leaving now.

642
01:03:21,885 --> 01:03:24,659
But soon your beloved
husband Ram will defeat...

643
01:03:24,862 --> 01:03:27,636
...Ravan and release
the people of Lanka.

644
01:03:27,839 --> 01:03:31,606
Take heart, be courageous, till
the day of liberty comes.

645
01:03:31,808 --> 01:03:34,582
Tell Ram to come and
save me quickly.

646
01:03:34,785 --> 01:03:37,559
I will be hopeful till then.
- I will surely tell him.

647
01:03:39,581 --> 01:03:43,506
Before I leave, I must teach
Ravan and his friends a lesson.

648
01:03:46,527 --> 01:03:49,470
Besides, I need the exercise.

649
01:04:01,412 --> 01:04:02,370
Douse the fire.

650
01:04:08,358 --> 01:04:10,309
The next one promises to be
a better match for me.

651
01:04:20,265 --> 01:04:22,216
Perhaps, if I let myself
to be captured...

652
01:04:23,242 --> 01:04:27,167
...I will be able to see Ravan
himself, face to face.

653
01:04:28,204 --> 01:04:30,154
Help! I can't stand the fire.

654
01:04:34,157 --> 01:04:37,100
You there!? What is
your name and...

655
01:04:37,300 --> 01:04:40,073
...who has sent you to Lanka?

656
01:04:46,230 --> 01:04:49,004
O Lord of Lanka, I am Hanuman.

657
01:04:49,207 --> 01:04:52,974
I come to you with respect as
a messenger of Lord Sugriva...

658
01:04:53,176 --> 01:04:57,936
...the Vanara King and devoted
friend of Ram, Prince of Ayodhya.

659
01:04:58,138 --> 01:05:01,905
You know it was a cowardly act
to carry off Princess Sita.

660
01:05:02,107 --> 01:05:03,888
Totally contrary to Dharm.

661
01:05:04,918 --> 01:05:06,869
This will surely end in
your destruction...

662
01:05:07,069 --> 01:05:08,850
...and the destruction
of your race.

663
01:05:10,872 --> 01:05:14,797
Restore Sita to the prince
and seek his forgiveness.

664
01:05:16,826 --> 01:05:18,777
Kill him.

665
01:05:20,795 --> 01:05:22,746
According to the law of kings,
you may mutilate, brand or whip...

666
01:05:22,945 --> 01:05:24,727
...a messenger, but kill him?

667
01:05:24,930 --> 01:05:28,697
Why? What's wrong in killing a
creature such as this?

668
01:05:28,899 --> 01:05:31,673
If you slay him, what
chance is there...

669
01:05:31,876 --> 01:05:33,657
...of our real enemies
being brought here?

670
01:05:34,853 --> 01:05:37,626
All right, but set fire to his
tail first. Then let him go home.

671
01:05:44,776 --> 01:05:47,549
Oh... it's hot. It's
burning me. Help!

672
01:05:52,548 --> 01:05:54,499
It's hot... it's hot...
it's hot...

673
01:05:55,525 --> 01:05:57,476
...it's hot... it's hot...
- Stop him! Stop him!

674
01:06:32,240 --> 01:06:35,183
Keep moving... keep moving,
friends... move forward.

675
01:06:36,209 --> 01:06:42,118
Victory awaits you!
Friends, keep moving.

676
01:06:42,329 --> 01:06:50,066
With Ram's name on
the lips, move ahead, friends.

677
01:06:50,267 --> 01:06:56,018
Keep moving... keep moving,
friends... move forward.

678
01:07:00,190 --> 01:07:03,957
The ray of the sun
is guiding our way.

679
01:07:04,986 --> 01:07:10,895
Gods believe that the demons
should be finished off.

680
01:07:12,924 --> 01:07:19,827
This is a war for the truth and
removal of the sins.

681
01:07:20,036 --> 01:07:26,780
The God of fire is with us,
move ahead, step-by-step.

682
01:07:26,982 --> 01:07:28,763
Keep moving, step-by-step.

683
01:07:30,785 --> 01:07:36,695
Keep moving... keep moving,
friends... move forward.

684
01:07:40,874 --> 01:07:44,641
The race of the demons is at
the verge of ruin.

685
01:07:44,843 --> 01:07:50,595
Finish off the evil with
the blows of your fists.

686
01:07:52,616 --> 01:07:55,559
This war is for justice.

687
01:07:56,751 --> 01:08:00,518
So be proud of yourself.

688
01:08:00,720 --> 01:08:08,457
With Ram's name on the lips,
move ahead, friends.

689
01:08:10,643 --> 01:08:16,394
Keep moving... keep moving
friends... move ahead.

690
01:08:31,315 --> 01:08:35,240
Ravan, my brother, I have come
to beg you. Return Sita...

691
01:08:35,450 --> 01:08:38,224
...to Ram or I fear the next
time not only the city...

692
01:08:38,427 --> 01:08:40,208
...but the palace itself
will go up in flames.

693
01:08:41,238 --> 01:08:46,155
You spoke this. If anyone else
had the gall to speak to me like...

694
01:08:46,365 --> 01:08:49,139
...this, I might have killed him
on the spot. I... King Ravan, who...

695
01:08:49,342 --> 01:08:52,116
...has won the obedience of all
men and the praises of the Gods ...

696
01:08:52,319 --> 01:08:57,078
...you expect me to shiver
from fear of a mere princeling?

697
01:08:57,280 --> 01:09:01,047
Be gone treacherous one.
Get out. Get out of my sight.

698
01:09:12,992 --> 01:09:15,935
Quiet! Quiet! How do we
cross over to the...

699
01:09:16,134 --> 01:09:18,908
...other side? - We will need
thousands of boats for these great troops.

700
01:09:19,938 --> 01:09:21,888
Then we can build a bridge.
- A bridge!? Do you know...

701
01:09:22,088 --> 01:09:24,861
...how many years it will take
to construct such a long bridge?

702
01:09:25,891 --> 01:09:28,835
If it is only mother Sita to be
rescued, I would fly to Lanka...

703
01:09:29,034 --> 01:09:31,807
...and accomplish the mission
myself quite easily.

704
01:09:32,011 --> 01:09:34,784
We have to rescue not only
Sita but others too.

705
01:09:34,988 --> 01:09:36,769
Ravan must be
destroyed or else...

706
01:09:36,972 --> 01:09:39,746
...there will be no lasting
peace on earth.

707
01:09:42,760 --> 01:09:45,703
Listen all of you. A demon,
named Vibhishana...

708
01:09:45,903 --> 01:09:48,676
...a brother of Ravan, comes
in peace, seeking refuge.

709
01:09:53,676 --> 01:09:57,600
He disagreed with his brother
and protected me in Ravan's palace.

710
01:09:57,810 --> 01:10:00,584
I have observed his honest
nature for myself.

711
01:10:00,787 --> 01:10:03,561
I see no fault in his
joining our forces.

712
01:10:03,764 --> 01:10:06,538
I agree with Hanuman.

713
01:10:07,568 --> 01:10:09,519
You are now amongst friends.

714
01:10:09,718 --> 01:10:11,499
Bless me, O Lord.

715
01:10:12,529 --> 01:10:16,454
I have overheard your
discussion on how to cross over...

716
01:10:16,664 --> 01:10:19,437
...to Lanka. I'd like to
suggest you pray to the Sea God for His help.

717
01:10:19,641 --> 01:10:21,422
That's good advice,
Vibhishana.

718
01:10:24,437 --> 01:10:27,380
For seven days and
seven nights...

719
01:10:27,579 --> 01:10:30,353
...Ram prayed to the Sea God.

720
01:10:35,352 --> 01:10:38,295
On the eighth dawn, the
God revealed Himself.

721
01:10:58,175 --> 01:11:03,091
Righteous Ram, build a
bridge with stones.

722
01:11:03,302 --> 01:11:07,069
Inscribe your name on each
stone and the stones will not...

723
01:11:07,271 --> 01:11:10,044
...sink in the ocean.

724
01:11:10,248 --> 01:11:13,021
Instead they will support
not only monkeys...

725
01:11:14,051 --> 01:11:16,994
...but all the living
creatures on the mountains<i>....</i>

726
01:11:18,020 --> 01:11:22,937
...and in the seas shall help
you build this bridge.

727
01:11:23,147 --> 01:11:25,921
And the Gods shall bless
you with success.

728
01:11:32,078 --> 01:11:35,845
Now... let's start! Let us
build the bridge.

729
01:11:36,874 --> 01:11:38,825
Hail! Hail!

730
01:11:39,024 --> 01:11:42,791
A bridge was built...

731
01:11:42,993 --> 01:11:47,753
...in the name of Ram.

732
01:11:48,781 --> 01:11:52,706
On the heart of the sea,
across the ocean...

733
01:11:53,743 --> 01:11:57,668
On the heart of the sea,
across the ocean...

734
01:11:58,704 --> 01:12:02,629
...a bridge was built...

735
01:12:03,666 --> 01:12:07,590
...in the name of Ram.

736
01:12:10,612 --> 01:12:14,536
All the stones and rocks...

737
01:12:15,573 --> 01:12:19,498
...were collected to
make the bridge.

738
01:12:19,708 --> 01:12:23,475
On the heart of the ocean...

739
01:12:23,677 --> 01:12:27,444
...they were laid...

740
01:12:27,646 --> 01:12:31,413
On the heart of the ocean...

741
01:12:31,616 --> 01:12:34,389
...they were laid...

742
01:12:34,593 --> 01:12:37,366
...with the blessings of the
feet of Raghupati (Ram)...

743
01:12:37,569 --> 01:12:39,351
...with the blessings of the
feet of Raghupati...

744
01:12:39,554 --> 01:12:42,328
...and by his mere touch...

745
01:12:42,531 --> 01:12:46,298
...the stones started
floating in the sea.

746
01:12:47,327 --> 01:12:50,270
A bridge was built...

747
01:12:51,296 --> 01:12:56,213
...in the name of Ram.

748
01:13:02,211 --> 01:13:06,136
Just as the
stones kept floating...

749
01:13:06,346 --> 01:13:13,090
...so does the name of Ram,
floats one in this sea of life.

750
01:13:14,119 --> 01:13:18,043
A remembrance of the
glorious tale of Ram...

751
01:13:19,080 --> 01:13:23,005
...a remembrance of the
glorious tale of Ram...

752
01:13:24,042 --> 01:13:27,966
...is sufficient to give
success in all the endeavors.

753
01:13:28,176 --> 01:13:32,936
Devotion towards Ram
is the key to success.

754
01:13:33,138 --> 01:13:37,897
Just the name of Ram is
enough to settle all matters.

755
01:13:38,926 --> 01:13:41,869
A bridge was built...

756
01:13:43,061 --> 01:13:46,828
...in the name of Ram.

757
01:13:48,022 --> 01:13:51,789
On the heart of the sea,
across the ocean, a bridge was built...

758
01:13:52,818 --> 01:13:56,743
...in the name of Ram.

759
01:14:01,914 --> 01:14:04,688
Members of the council,
we are facing...

760
01:14:04,891 --> 01:14:07,665
...an outbreak of war.

761
01:14:07,868 --> 01:14:09,649
What do you have
to say, Prahastha?

762
01:14:10,679 --> 01:14:14,604
Your Majesty, you as the
great lord of Lanka...

763
01:14:14,814 --> 01:14:18,581
...need not have called this
council just to consider...

764
01:14:18,783 --> 01:14:22,550
...this ridiculous threat, from
a handful of men and monkeys.

765
01:14:23,579 --> 01:14:26,522
Just send a couple of my men...

766
01:14:26,722 --> 01:14:28,503
...who are not even present
in this council...

767
01:14:29,533 --> 01:14:32,476
...and they will surely
wipe out Ram's army.

768
01:14:32,675 --> 01:14:34,457
Ravan...

769
01:14:34,660 --> 01:14:38,427
...I told you before but now I
have to repeat it. Those who...

770
01:14:38,629 --> 01:14:43,388
...govern the kingdom should
never be swayed by flattery.

771
01:14:44,417 --> 01:14:47,360
The armies attacking us are
no ordinary ones.

772
01:14:48,386 --> 01:14:51,330
Ravan, I will tell you this
for your own good.

773
01:14:52,356 --> 01:14:55,299
Return Sita, she is the wife
of the Prince of Ayodhya.

774
01:14:55,498 --> 01:14:57,279
Grandfather...

775
01:14:59,302 --> 01:15:03,226
...why do we have to return
her now? If we release her now...

776
01:15:03,436 --> 01:15:07,203
...they will think that we
are all afraid of fighting.

777
01:15:08,232 --> 01:15:11,175
That is not so!? I cannot
bear the sight of...

778
01:15:11,375 --> 01:15:15,142
...so many people injured
and even more dead...

779
01:15:16,171 --> 01:15:18,122
...just for this one woman.

780
01:15:18,321 --> 01:15:22,088
Grandfather, that means you
are afraid of fighting.

781
01:15:23,117 --> 01:15:26,060
If you are scared of bloodshed
how can you fight?

782
01:15:26,259 --> 01:15:30,026
Indrajeet, I am no coward.

783
01:15:30,228 --> 01:15:33,995
But yes, I don't want
to fight unnecessarily.

784
01:15:36,017 --> 01:15:40,933
You called me, O Ram.
- Yes, brave Prince of the Vanaras...

785
01:15:41,144 --> 01:15:43,917
...please, listen to what
I have to say, carefully.

786
01:15:46,932 --> 01:15:48,883
For these many months...

787
01:15:49,082 --> 01:15:50,863
...I've been thinking of
only defeating Ravan.

788
01:15:51,066 --> 01:15:53,840
Now my dream is about to
come true, however...

789
01:15:55,862 --> 01:15:59,787
...I have considered this matter
over and over again and...

790
01:16:00,989 --> 01:16:04,756
...I've concluded that I can
stop this fight even now...

791
01:16:04,959 --> 01:16:08,725
...if my wife Sita and other
captives are released...

792
01:16:08,928 --> 01:16:11,701
...and they ask for
shelter under me.

793
01:16:14,716 --> 01:16:17,659
Quiet! - You are, no
doubt, surprised, but...

794
01:16:18,685 --> 01:16:20,636
... shedding of blood
should be avoided...

795
01:16:20,835 --> 01:16:23,609
... and real peace should come
back to the three worlds.

796
01:16:23,812 --> 01:16:25,593
To ensure this...

797
01:16:25,797 --> 01:16:28,570
...I am ready to forgive and
forget the misdeeds of Ravan.

798
01:16:29,600 --> 01:16:32,543
Angad, could you carry
this message to Ravan?

799
01:16:36,546 --> 01:16:39,490
I... I understand. I will
surely convey your message...

800
01:16:39,689 --> 01:16:41,470
...to Ravan.
- Thank you, Angad.

801
01:16:49,446 --> 01:16:52,389
Is that all you
have to say to me?

802
01:16:53,415 --> 01:16:57,340
Well... Angad... that's
your name, isn't it?

803
01:16:58,377 --> 01:17:00,328
Here is my answer.

804
01:17:02,512 --> 01:17:04,293
How despicable!

805
01:17:04,496 --> 01:17:07,270
Is this how you treat a
messenger who comes in peace?

806
01:17:18,223 --> 01:17:19,181
Ravan...

807
01:17:21,200 --> 01:17:25,124
...Ravan, I have your answer.
And now I will carry your answer...

808
01:17:25,334 --> 01:17:29,101
...to Ram. Next time I see you,
it will be on the battlefield.

809
01:17:32,115 --> 01:17:35,058
So, Ravan wants war, after all.

810
01:17:35,257 --> 01:17:38,031
I understand. Angad,
I appreciate your endeavor.

811
01:17:38,234 --> 01:17:41,008
I am sorry, Ram,
but Ravan did not accept...

812
01:17:41,211 --> 01:17:43,985
...your message of peace.
I did my best.

813
01:17:50,142 --> 01:17:52,915
Now, tomorrow morning...

814
01:17:53,118 --> 01:17:54,900
...when the first rays of the
sun touch the mountaintops...

815
01:17:55,930 --> 01:17:57,881
...the battle will begin.

816
01:17:58,080 --> 01:17:59,861
I ask all of you present here...

817
01:18:00,891 --> 01:18:04,816
...will you fight for
justice and for Ram?

818
01:18:05,026 --> 01:18:08,793
All hail to Ram!
All hail to Sugriva!

819
01:18:08,995 --> 01:18:11,769
Hail! Hail! Hail!

820
01:18:55,467 --> 01:18:58,411
Hail to the great
lord of Lanka.

821
01:18:59,437 --> 01:19:02,380
Hail to the great
lord of Lanka.

822
01:19:03,406 --> 01:19:07,330
If anyone tries to get in
a scuffle with Ravan...

823
01:19:07,540 --> 01:19:11,307
If anyone tries to get in
a scuffle with Ravan...

824
01:19:11,510 --> 01:19:16,269
...he is sure to die
a dog's death.

825
01:19:16,471 --> 01:19:20,238
...he is sure to die
a dog's death.

826
01:19:20,440 --> 01:19:24,207
Hail to the king who
has ten lives.

827
01:19:25,236 --> 01:19:28,179
Hail to the king who
has ten lives.

828
01:19:31,190 --> 01:19:35,114
He kills all his
enemies in no time.

829
01:19:35,325 --> 01:19:39,092
He kills all the enemies!

830
01:19:39,294 --> 01:19:43,061
Hail to the king of demons!

831
01:19:43,263 --> 01:19:48,022
Hail to the king of demons!

832
01:19:51,036 --> 01:19:54,960
I pray to you, O Gods,
I pray to you.

833
01:19:55,997 --> 01:19:59,922
Please... please... protect Ram.
Protect my husband.

834
01:20:56,527 --> 01:20:58,478
Oh, what a nuisance!
This is bothering me.

835
01:21:37,377 --> 01:21:39,158
The day began well
for us, O King.

836
01:21:39,361 --> 01:21:43,128
But now the two armies
seem equally matched.

837
01:21:43,330 --> 01:21:45,112
Our men are beginning to tire.

838
01:21:46,142 --> 01:21:50,066
Let them withdraw
at once then and rest.

839
01:21:50,276 --> 01:21:54,043
Respected one, that will
only lead to our defeat.

840
01:21:54,246 --> 01:21:58,013
Let us send Kumbhakarna's sons,
Kumbha and Nikumbha.

841
01:21:59,041 --> 01:22:00,992
Tired soldiers can
fall back to defense...

842
01:22:01,192 --> 01:22:03,965
...but we shall keep up
pressure on our enemies...

843
01:22:04,168 --> 01:22:06,942
...until sunset. - Yes, at
sunset, Ram will stop the battle...

844
01:22:07,145 --> 01:22:11,905
...for the day to
attend to the wounded...

845
01:22:12,107 --> 01:22:15,874
...and to cremate the
dead with honor. - Good.

846
01:22:16,076 --> 01:22:18,931
I will send forth
Kumbha and Nikumbha.

847
01:22:25,403 --> 01:22:28,318
Here I come...
monkeys, down with you.

848
01:22:31,487 --> 01:22:33,538
I will crush you to crumbs.

849
01:22:37,745 --> 01:22:39,796
O my God!

850
01:23:01,735 --> 01:23:03,785
Monkeys...

851
01:23:04,864 --> 01:23:06,914
...I will kill you.

852
01:23:17,554 --> 01:23:20,470
Your Majesty,
Kumbha and Nikumbha...

853
01:23:20,683 --> 01:23:23,599
...are fighting with great
courage on the battlefield.

854
01:23:23,812 --> 01:23:27,772
Well, after all, they are
the sons of Kumbhakarna.

855
01:23:31,982 --> 01:23:34,033
So many dead!

856
01:23:35,111 --> 01:23:37,162
So many wounded!

857
01:23:42,413 --> 01:23:45,506
Have you got the
water ready? - Yes.

858
01:23:45,716 --> 01:23:47,588
Medicines? Herbs?
- Yes, they are ready.

859
01:23:48,671 --> 01:23:51,764
Let's get the bed set fast.
C'mon quickly. - Yeah.

860
01:24:02,404 --> 01:24:05,320
Hey, more herbs.

861
01:24:06,402 --> 01:24:08,453
There are so many wounded.

862
01:24:27,263 --> 01:24:31,388
You've fought bravely.
I am so proud of you.

863
01:24:32,478 --> 01:24:35,572
Now rest. - Oh no.
Such a tiny wound...

864
01:24:35,781 --> 01:24:38,696
...will be cured by
tomorrow, you will see.

865
01:24:41,865 --> 01:24:45,990
Do not strain yourself,
rest. - Yes... yes, sir.

866
01:25:01,857 --> 01:25:04,772
Brother, how could you
cremate the bodies of our...

867
01:25:04,986 --> 01:25:06,858
...enemies along with those
of our own soldiers?

868
01:25:07,941 --> 01:25:12,066
Lakshman, they were our men and
Ravan's men while they were alive.

869
01:25:12,287 --> 01:25:15,202
But in death they
are no longer enemies.

870
01:25:15,416 --> 01:25:18,331
Do they not all of them deserve
a solemn cremation?

871
01:25:19,414 --> 01:25:21,465
It is not like a true warrior...

872
01:25:21,674 --> 01:25:24,590
...a true Kshatriya, to be
moved by such emotions.

873
01:25:24,803 --> 01:25:28,763
My brother, when we set out
on this expedition...

874
01:25:30,018 --> 01:25:32,934
...I too was full
of anger, bitterness.

875
01:25:33,147 --> 01:25:36,063
But on our journey to Lanka,
I've come to see that all of us...

876
01:25:37,145 --> 01:25:41,271
...have received the precious
gift of life from the Gods.

877
01:25:42,535 --> 01:25:45,450
And it is more important to
be a good human being...

878
01:25:45,664 --> 01:25:48,579
...then to just be
a good Kshatriya.

879
01:25:49,836 --> 01:25:53,795
Have we not, all of us,
sprung from the same souls?

880
01:25:54,008 --> 01:25:56,923
Rakshash, vanar, men, beasts...

881
01:25:57,137 --> 01:26:00,052
...birds of the air,
the fish of the ocean...??

882
01:26:03,221 --> 01:26:06,315
Yet, some of us, in ignorance...

883
01:26:06,524 --> 01:26:09,440
...draw their bows and swords
against their fellow creatures.

884
01:26:11,565 --> 01:26:13,616
Many have fallen off
this battlefield today.

885
01:26:13,825 --> 01:26:16,741
And many more shall die
before the war is done.

886
01:26:16,954 --> 01:26:20,914
And as a Kshatriya, I shall
continue to fight my battles.

887
01:26:23,039 --> 01:26:26,132
But when I burn
the dead, I shall pray...

888
01:26:26,342 --> 01:26:29,257
...for a world free
from all wars.

889
01:26:30,340 --> 01:26:33,433
That a man does not
raise his hand in anger...

890
01:26:33,643 --> 01:26:35,515
...against his own brother.

891
01:26:39,727 --> 01:26:41,778
Brother, words fail me.

892
01:27:17,276 --> 01:27:20,370
I am Neel, the General
of the Vanaras.

893
01:27:20,579 --> 01:27:23,495
Try all you can.
I shall defeat you.

894
01:28:13,599 --> 01:28:17,725
You have fought well
but this is the end.

895
01:28:51,148 --> 01:28:52,156
Wait!

896
01:28:59,666 --> 01:29:02,582
Hail Sugriva! Hail Sugriva!

897
01:29:48,515 --> 01:29:51,608
Kumbha, Kumbha... my brother.

898
01:29:53,730 --> 01:29:55,780
Are you really gone?

899
01:30:00,162 --> 01:30:04,122
Is it you? Is it you who
killed my brother Kumbha?

900
01:30:05,203 --> 01:30:09,328
Yes, I am... I am Sugriva,
the king of the Vanaras.

901
01:30:09,549 --> 01:30:13,509
Your brother Kumbha was
really brave and courageous.

902
01:30:15,633 --> 01:30:18,727
I have never met such a
mighty opponent before.

903
01:30:18,936 --> 01:30:22,896
I am very impressed by his
tactics. Please cremate him in honor.

904
01:30:23,978 --> 01:30:27,071
Indrajeet, what are you
saying? Prahastha and Kumbha...

905
01:30:27,281 --> 01:30:30,196
...both have been killed?
- It is unfortunate but true.

906
01:30:33,365 --> 01:30:35,415
I never thought Ram's army
had anyone to match them.

907
01:30:36,494 --> 01:30:39,588
It's time to review our
strategy. It can be of help under the...

908
01:30:39,797 --> 01:30:42,712
...circumstances. Indrajeet,
arouse Kumbhakarna from his sleep.

909
01:30:42,926 --> 01:30:45,842
What? - Kumbha and Nikumbha
fought so hard.

910
01:30:46,055 --> 01:30:51,058
Now Kumbhakarna, their father,
ten times mightier than...

911
01:30:51,270 --> 01:30:54,186
...them can work wonders.
Yes, I am right, wake him up...

912
01:30:54,399 --> 01:30:56,272
...immediately.
This is my command.

913
01:30:56,485 --> 01:30:58,358
All right, father. I will.

914
01:31:08,828 --> 01:31:10,878
Forward.

915
01:32:09,323 --> 01:32:11,374
C'mon... yeah...

916
01:32:34,530 --> 01:32:35,359
Oh, that big giant!

917
01:32:36,442 --> 01:32:38,492
Our lord
Kumbhakarna has arrived.

918
01:32:56,259 --> 01:32:59,353
Father... father!

919
01:33:11,905 --> 01:33:14,998
Vibhishana, who is that
gigantic warrior? - That O Ram, is the...

920
01:33:15,208 --> 01:33:21,253
...best and the bravest
warrior of Ravan's troops. Kumbhakarna...

921
01:33:23,552 --> 01:33:26,467
...after six months' sleep, he
would have become immortal.

922
01:33:27,550 --> 01:33:31,675
But it seems to me that Ravan
was forced to wake up because...

923
01:33:31,896 --> 01:33:35,856
...he was in terror to see so
many of his soldiers killed one...

924
01:33:36,068 --> 01:33:40,028
...after the other. Oh yes, he
needs Kumbhakarna. But even he is...

925
01:33:40,240 --> 01:33:42,113
...not immortal. He is mighty
enough to make all the...

926
01:33:42,326 --> 01:33:44,199
... vanara soldiers run
away in panic...

927
01:33:44,413 --> 01:33:47,328
...by his appearance. But Ram...

928
01:33:47,542 --> 01:33:50,457
...now is the right moment for
you to go to battle.

929
01:33:53,278 --> 01:33:55,328
Now, we go to battle.

930
01:35:08,550 --> 01:35:10,422
Jump!

931
01:35:20,892 --> 01:35:23,986
Stop that!

932
01:35:25,064 --> 01:35:27,115
You are small but
you have courage.

933
01:35:31,322 --> 01:35:35,447
I am Angad, son of Bali.
The nephew of king Sugriva.

934
01:35:35,668 --> 01:35:38,584
You are kinsmen
of the Vanara king!?

935
01:35:39,666 --> 01:35:43,792
No wonder you fight so great.
But this is as far as you get...

936
01:35:44,012 --> 01:35:45,885
...against me. - Wait.

937
01:35:49,228 --> 01:35:54,230
This is now my mission.
I see you are Kumbhakarna.

938
01:35:54,443 --> 01:35:57,358
The mightiest warrior of Lanka.

939
01:35:57,572 --> 01:36:01,531
Now this Hanuman
is your opponent.

940
01:36:01,744 --> 01:36:04,659
Good... Good.

941
01:36:05,742 --> 01:36:07,793
But before we fight... here.

942
01:36:13,043 --> 01:36:16,137
Oh... Kumbha...
Nikumbha... my sons.

943
01:36:25,559 --> 01:36:31,771
Hanuman, I thank you for your
consideration. - It is nothing.

944
01:36:42,248 --> 01:36:44,298
I won't fight you with
bare hands because...

945
01:36:44,508 --> 01:36:48,467
...you are skillful enough to
fight with weapons in dead earnest.

946
01:37:30,401 --> 01:37:33,317
It was good for you
that I lost my mace.

947
01:37:33,530 --> 01:37:35,403
Now get up and fight.

948
01:37:35,616 --> 01:37:38,532
Wait... stop wherever you are.

949
01:37:38,745 --> 01:37:42,705
I am Ram, the Prince of
Ayodhya, son of Dashrath.

950
01:37:59,432 --> 01:38:01,482
Give away, you stupid fools!

951
01:38:02,735 --> 01:38:05,650
So you are Ram!?

952
01:38:06,733 --> 01:38:09,827
You are a skillful
swordsman, I hear.

953
01:38:10,036 --> 01:38:11,908
You are annoying me.

954
01:38:12,991 --> 01:38:16,085
Go away, play
with the monkeys.

955
01:38:25,507 --> 01:38:29,633
It has grown dark
and even with...

956
01:38:29,854 --> 01:38:32,769
...Kumbhakarna on the field the
battle goes on and on.

957
01:38:32,983 --> 01:38:35,898
Father, I will go to the
battlefield and bring you the report.

958
01:38:36,112 --> 01:38:37,984
Yes Indrajeet, my son, go.

959
01:39:11,401 --> 01:39:15,526
Excuse me Kumbhakarna,
I am only doing my duty.

960
01:39:34,347 --> 01:39:36,398
He has done it!
He has done it.

961
01:39:37,476 --> 01:39:39,527
Hail to the Prince of Ayodhya!

962
01:39:41,648 --> 01:39:45,774
Brother, are you well?
It has been a glorious deed!

963
01:39:46,863 --> 01:39:50,989
Yes... I am hurt but
well in spirit.

964
01:39:51,210 --> 01:39:54,125
I wish I had known
him as a friend.

965
01:39:54,339 --> 01:39:57,254
Vibhishana, I am sorry,
Kumbhakarna had to die at my hands.

966
01:40:06,681 --> 01:40:09,775
Save us... save us O Vanaras.

967
01:40:17,111 --> 01:40:20,205
Thank you, Lord Ram!

968
01:40:20,414 --> 01:40:22,287
Ram, the great!

969
01:40:23,369 --> 01:40:26,463
Freedom, at last!

970
01:40:28,584 --> 01:40:30,635
We are free!

971
01:40:30,845 --> 01:40:33,760
What? Even
Kumbhakarna is gone?

972
01:40:33,974 --> 01:40:36,889
This spells
disaster for Lanka.

973
01:40:37,103 --> 01:40:40,018
He was a fine warrior.

974
01:40:41,101 --> 01:40:44,194
It is sad, very sad.

975
01:40:44,404 --> 01:40:47,319
Father... don't despair.
Have faith.

976
01:40:47,533 --> 01:40:50,448
I have a plan.

977
01:40:50,662 --> 01:40:54,622
I will devastate Ram's troops.
I assure you of this.

978
01:40:55,703 --> 01:40:59,828
Well said, my son, well said.
My faith lies in you.

979
01:41:00,918 --> 01:41:02,969
Now go ahead. - Yes, father.

980
01:41:04,221 --> 01:41:07,137
Let us bring all of them in,
while it is still dark.

981
01:41:07,350 --> 01:41:09,223
Hurry... hurry.

982
01:41:13,609 --> 01:41:17,568
There will be many more
corpses for you to gather, my friend.

983
01:41:17,781 --> 01:41:21,740
How dare he speak this way?
I will show him.

984
01:41:21,953 --> 01:41:23,825
Wait! What is that?

985
01:41:28,211 --> 01:41:30,083
That is Sita.

986
01:41:36,381 --> 01:41:39,475
Hanuman, are you
alright? Angad!?

987
01:41:47,854 --> 01:41:51,980
Where is Ram?
Why is he such a coward?

988
01:41:54,113 --> 01:41:57,206
Ram... Ram...

989
01:41:58,285 --> 01:42:00,335
Sita... my queen!

990
01:42:02,457 --> 01:42:04,507
Here you are.

991
01:42:05,760 --> 01:42:07,632
Ram, watch carefully.

992
01:42:14,104 --> 01:42:18,064
Stop! Stop! STOP!

993
01:42:23,491 --> 01:42:28,494
Sita... Sita!

994
01:42:41,223 --> 01:42:43,095
Lakshman...

995
01:42:43,309 --> 01:42:46,224
...come... come...
come over here.

996
01:42:53,739 --> 01:42:57,699
Before I dispose of you, Ram,
I will give you...

997
01:42:57,911 --> 01:43:01,871
...enough time to hold a funeral
for your wife and your brother.

998
01:43:10,427 --> 01:43:12,300
Sita!

999
01:43:20,858 --> 01:43:23,773
May I talk with
you for a moment?

1000
01:43:23,987 --> 01:43:27,946
We have almost used up all the
herbs around in this area.

1001
01:43:28,159 --> 01:43:32,118
But they don't heal the wounds
inflicted by Indrajeet, at all.

1002
01:43:32,331 --> 01:43:36,291
What? What news
is this? - O God!

1003
01:43:37,372 --> 01:43:41,497
Oh... I have already lost
my beloved wife Sita...

1004
01:43:41,718 --> 01:43:45,678
...and now... I am going to lose
my dear, dear brother, Lakshman.

1005
01:43:46,759 --> 01:43:48,810
If I lose him, what else
would be left for me?

1006
01:43:51,974 --> 01:43:55,068
Brace yourself, Ram. You
cannot grieve and fret like this.

1007
01:43:55,278 --> 01:43:58,193
Your despair will damage the
morale of our troops more than the...

1008
01:43:58,407 --> 01:44:02,366
...enemy's arrows. Please
do not worry, Ram.

1009
01:44:02,579 --> 01:44:05,494
Sita surely must be alive.
- Alive? But I saw Sita...

1010
01:44:05,708 --> 01:44:09,667
...slain before my own eyes.

1011
01:44:09,880 --> 01:44:13,839
I know, it must be one of
Indrajeet's magic tricks.

1012
01:44:14,052 --> 01:44:16,967
A magic trick? What? - Yes.

1013
01:44:17,181 --> 01:44:20,097
And we must not allow his
tricks to perplex us.

1014
01:44:20,310 --> 01:44:22,183
Your grief will only
give him strength.

1015
01:44:23,265 --> 01:44:27,390
Indrajeet's strength lies
in his magical powers.

1016
01:44:27,611 --> 01:44:31,571
The only way to take his
powers away from him is to...

1017
01:44:31,783 --> 01:44:34,699
...attack Indrajeet while he
performs his Tantrik rites...

1018
01:44:34,808 --> 01:44:35,744
...in the cave of Nikumbhila.

1019
01:44:35,956 --> 01:44:39,915
Indrajeet makes it a rule to
perform a religious ceremony.

1020
01:44:40,128 --> 01:44:43,043
He offers sacrifices to
the Goddess Nikumbhila.

1021
01:44:43,257 --> 01:44:46,172
From the evening hours
way until nightfall.

1022
01:44:46,386 --> 01:44:50,345
He gains his extraordinary
magical powers through this ceremony.

1023
01:44:51,427 --> 01:44:55,552
I see, now... we still have so many...

1024
01:44:55,773 --> 01:44:58,689
...soldiers wounded, my
brother Lakshman, for instance.

1025
01:44:59,771 --> 01:45:03,896
No, I think it would be very
hard for us to attack Nikumbhila...

1026
01:45:04,117 --> 01:45:05,990
...cave now. - Ram.

1027
01:45:08,115 --> 01:45:12,241
In... in the Himalayas...
- Yes the Himalayas...

1028
01:45:12,461 --> 01:45:16,421
... what about them? Rest,
Jamvant. Talk to me.

1029
01:45:18,546 --> 01:45:21,639
I know there are
some herbs there...

1030
01:45:22,718 --> 01:45:26,843
...that can heal our wounds,
in the Himalayas. - The Himalayas?

1031
01:45:29,150 --> 01:45:32,065
I am afraid... I am afraid
that is too far away.

1032
01:46:21,127 --> 01:46:26,295
I see... that must be
Ram's kingdom! Ayodhya!

1033
01:46:34,686 --> 01:46:36,737
The Himalayas!

1034
01:46:39,902 --> 01:46:41,952
O you Himalayas!

1035
01:46:43,205 --> 01:46:47,164
Sacred mountains! At last!

1036
01:47:37,268 --> 01:47:39,319
Ah Dronagiri, at last!

1037
01:47:48,915 --> 01:47:51,831
Now, I have to look for herbs.

1038
01:47:52,044 --> 01:47:54,960
Our army is in
desperate need of this.

1039
01:48:00,389 --> 01:48:03,304
Ah the herbs... there they are.

1040
01:48:10,819 --> 01:48:13,734
Uff... that was painful.

1041
01:48:27,507 --> 01:48:31,467
Good, the pain is gone.
I am healed.

1042
01:48:31,679 --> 01:48:35,639
These herbs were far better
than I ever expected.

1043
01:48:40,893 --> 01:48:43,986
But wait! Just a
handful of these herbs...

1044
01:48:44,196 --> 01:48:47,111
...won't be enough
to heal them all.

1045
01:48:49,237 --> 01:48:52,330
Now... let me think.

1046
01:48:58,624 --> 01:49:01,718
I will take one.
Yes, this tree is good enough.

1047
01:49:43,648 --> 01:49:45,521
This will be a landmark.

1048
01:49:57,033 --> 01:50:00,127
Now I will pick up...

1049
01:50:00,337 --> 01:50:03,252
...the whole mountain.

1050
01:50:36,668 --> 01:50:40,794
I pray to you O Gods!
Protect my master Lakshman...

1051
01:50:41,015 --> 01:50:42,887
...I am coming back
with the herbs.

1052
01:50:45,187 --> 01:50:50,189
Brother Lakshman, keep up
your fight for life a little longer.

1053
01:50:57,529 --> 01:51:00,623
Bear your pain with courage,
Lakshman. Take heart...

1054
01:51:00,832 --> 01:51:03,748
...Hanuman will soon be back
with the herbs that will heal you.

1055
01:51:11,088 --> 01:51:16,257
Ram... Ram...
- Lakshman... Lakshman.

1056
01:51:17,346 --> 01:51:21,472
There he is.
- Hanuman has come. - Hail! Hail!

1057
01:51:22,562 --> 01:51:26,687
Here comes Hanuman! - But
what has he got on his shoulders?

1058
01:51:27,777 --> 01:51:30,870
He is carrying something.
- That's a mountain he is carrying.

1059
01:51:31,080 --> 01:51:35,039
Along with the herbs, he has
brought the whole mountain.

1060
01:51:53,852 --> 01:51:56,946
Hanuman, the herbs are on
this mountain? - Yes.

1061
01:51:57,155 --> 01:52:01,115
Look for the landmarks where
I have stuck trees to the soil.

1062
01:52:01,328 --> 01:52:04,243
Hurry, apply the herbs
to Lakshman's wounds.

1063
01:52:05,326 --> 01:52:08,419
Yes, it's a miracle.

1064
01:52:14,713 --> 01:52:17,807
Herbs... herbs. - At last.

1065
01:52:26,186 --> 01:52:29,280
Brother Ram... - O Lakshman...

1066
01:52:29,489 --> 01:52:31,362
...you have
regained consciousness.

1067
01:52:35,747 --> 01:52:38,663
Hanuman, you too are a
beloved brother to me.

1068
01:52:46,004 --> 01:52:49,097
Hey... - Who is that?

1069
01:53:04,778 --> 01:53:06,829
Hey... what was that?

1070
01:53:14,165 --> 01:53:16,216
C'mon... c'mon.

1071
01:53:58,146 --> 01:54:00,019
What has happened?

1072
01:54:02,145 --> 01:54:04,195
Oh no... who is there?

1073
01:54:05,274 --> 01:54:08,367
Is it you? You are still alive.

1074
01:54:09,446 --> 01:54:14,614
Yes, and it is time for you
to die along with your guardian Goddess.

1075
01:54:19,007 --> 01:54:21,922
It is hard to believe
that even such one as you...

1076
01:54:22,136 --> 01:54:24,008
...can have faithful
slaves to save you.

1077
01:54:25,091 --> 01:54:28,185
All of you, kill him.

1078
01:54:59,511 --> 01:55:01,562
What a nuisance!

1079
01:55:07,855 --> 01:55:09,906
You... take me up there!

1080
01:55:42,275 --> 01:55:44,326
Indrajeet... - I am...

1081
01:55:44,535 --> 01:55:48,495
...not so stupid to be trapped
by a monkey like you!

1082
01:55:57,920 --> 01:55:59,971
He has slipped past.

1083
01:56:10,437 --> 01:56:14,562
Listen, you obey my commands
and I'll spare your life.

1084
01:56:14,783 --> 01:56:16,655
Carry me to the sky. Remember...

1085
01:56:16,869 --> 01:56:18,741
...you should head right,
when I say right...

1086
01:56:18,955 --> 01:56:21,870
...and left when I say left.
If you fail to do so...

1087
01:56:22,084 --> 01:56:24,999
...this sword
will cut your throat.

1088
01:56:47,986 --> 01:56:50,036
Lakshman... !!?

1089
01:56:51,115 --> 01:56:54,208
Just keep going...
and faster... faster.

1090
01:56:55,287 --> 01:56:57,337
I will kill you.

1091
01:57:01,545 --> 01:57:03,596
Not this time.
This time I will kill you.

1092
01:57:17,190 --> 01:57:19,241
You cannot destroy this.

1093
01:57:30,924 --> 01:57:34,883
But this is the end of you.

1094
01:57:37,008 --> 01:57:39,058
This is your end, not mine.

1095
01:57:43,266 --> 01:57:45,317
I've waited for this moment.

1096
01:57:50,567 --> 01:57:52,618
Got you, you little one.

1097
01:58:11,428 --> 01:58:14,521
This is the end of
the invincible Indrajeet.

1098
01:58:16,643 --> 01:58:20,768
No... never...
I wouldn't let you kill me.

1099
01:58:40,632 --> 01:58:43,726
O Indrajeet... my son.

1100
01:58:43,935 --> 01:58:47,895
My beloved son slew
an illusion of Sita.

1101
01:58:48,108 --> 01:58:51,023
I shall not slay the real one.

1102
01:58:51,237 --> 01:58:55,196
Anyone so devoted to
Ram deserves to die.

1103
01:58:56,278 --> 01:58:59,371
Will you now add to your
sins by killing Sita!?

1104
01:58:59,581 --> 01:59:01,453
An innocent woman!?

1105
01:59:01,667 --> 01:59:05,626
Look at Prahastha, look
at Kumbha... Nikumbha...

1106
01:59:05,839 --> 01:59:08,754
...and Kumbhakarna.
Each one fought bravely and...

1107
01:59:08,968 --> 01:59:10,841
...died a hero's death.
Even Indrajeet died...

1108
01:59:11,054 --> 01:59:15,014
...in battle. You who
are brother, father...

1109
01:59:15,226 --> 01:59:18,142
...king to them all...

1110
01:59:18,355 --> 01:59:20,228
...do you want
disgrace their memory?

1111
01:59:20,441 --> 01:59:23,357
The time has
come for both of us...

1112
01:59:23,570 --> 01:59:25,443
...to go forth
and avenge our kinsmen.

1113
01:59:27,569 --> 01:59:30,662
I understand. But you will stay
here and protect our women and...

1114
01:59:30,872 --> 01:59:33,787
...children. No power on earth
can crush me. Not even Ram's.

1115
02:00:28,064 --> 02:00:30,115
Fire and damnation!

1116
02:00:51,011 --> 02:00:53,061
He looks like Vishnu
himself on his Garuda.

1117
02:00:53,271 --> 02:00:55,143
You are right, he does.

1118
02:01:31,689 --> 02:01:35,814
This battle between you and
me shall be the end of it all.

1119
02:01:36,035 --> 02:01:38,950
Citizens of Lanka, take heed.

1120
02:01:40,033 --> 02:01:43,126
Your king Ravan, whom you
consider a symbol of eternal...

1121
02:01:43,336 --> 02:01:47,295
...power, watch him die at
the hands of a mere mortal.

1122
02:01:48,377 --> 02:01:52,502
Ram, just tell me where your
conceit comes from, huh?

1123
02:01:52,723 --> 02:01:56,683
Your boastful lips will never
speak such words again.

1124
02:01:56,895 --> 02:01:59,811
Brave soldiers of Lanka...

1125
02:02:00,024 --> 02:02:01,897
...you know only too well...

1126
02:02:02,110 --> 02:02:05,026
...who is the mightiest
of all, here!

1127
02:02:05,239 --> 02:02:08,155
C'mon Ran...

1128
02:02:08,369 --> 02:02:11,284
So be it, Ravan! Fight!

1129
02:03:02,432 --> 02:03:04,482
Incredible!

1130
02:03:10,950 --> 02:03:12,823
Now, he is dead.

1131
02:03:35,809 --> 02:03:38,902
I can't believe my own eyes.

1132
02:03:43,110 --> 02:03:45,160
You thought I was
finished, did you?

1133
02:03:48,325 --> 02:03:51,419
I would like to
lay my hands on you!

1134
02:04:18,573 --> 02:04:20,623
Let's see you
get out of that one.

1135
02:04:40,476 --> 02:04:43,570
What power is
this, greater than mine?

1136
02:04:52,124 --> 02:04:55,039
Oh, you are going
too far now, I tell you.

1137
02:05:19,068 --> 02:05:21,119
Don't you dare!

1138
02:05:26,369 --> 02:05:28,420
Give up, Ram... give up!

1139
02:05:55,574 --> 02:05:58,668
Om... peace... peace... peace!!!

1140
02:06:46,682 --> 02:06:51,851
May you rest in peace,
brother Ravan. - It is all over.

1141
02:06:59,199 --> 02:07:04,367
Soldiers of Lanka, king Ravan
has gone back to mother Earth.

1142
02:07:05,457 --> 02:07:07,507
Give up fighting.
Lay down your arms...

1143
02:07:07,717 --> 02:07:11,676
...and devote yourself to
restoring the glory of your country...

1144
02:07:11,889 --> 02:07:16,749
...with your new king Vibhishana.

1145
02:07:20,791 --> 02:07:22,759
Ram...

1146
02:07:36,807 --> 02:07:38,775
Sita! - Ram!

1147
02:07:48,819 --> 02:07:52,778
Thank you all, but when I think
of the people who died for me...

1148
02:07:53,824 --> 02:07:56,793
...I feel sad. I will meditate
and will pray for them from now on...

1149
02:07:56,994 --> 02:07:58,791
...and beg their forgiveness.

1150
02:07:59,830 --> 02:08:01,798
You don't need to do that.

1151
02:08:01,999 --> 02:08:04,797
All you need is to live
in peace with Ram...

1152
02:08:05,002 --> 02:08:06,799
...to make their death
a glorious sacrifice.

1153
02:08:07,004 --> 02:08:09,802
I will remember
what you said, Sugriva.

1154
02:08:12,843 --> 02:08:16,802
Vibhishana, the new king of
Lanka presents Ram and Sita...

1155
02:08:17,014 --> 02:08:19,812
... the Vimana, the flying
chariot, to return to Ayodhya.

1156
02:08:42,873 --> 02:08:46,832
As they return, Sita gazes
at Ram with mixed feelings.

1157
02:08:47,044 --> 02:08:49,842
Happy to be
reunited with him...

1158
02:08:50,047 --> 02:08:51,844
...after a long
period of separation.

1159
02:08:52,049 --> 02:08:55,849
And sorrowful too for the
precious lives lost for her sake...

1160
02:08:56,053 --> 02:08:57,850
...in the avoidable war.

1161
02:09:08,899 --> 02:09:11,868
Ayodhya celebrates the safe
return of their beloved king...

1162
02:09:12,069 --> 02:09:14,867
...and they live
happily thereafter.

1163
02:09:15,072 --> 02:09:17,870
A few years later,
Ram returns to the Heavens...

1164
02:09:18,075 --> 02:09:19,872
...while Sita
returns to Mother Earth.

